he user's request, they want to bind \"泵1\" (pump 1) to \"马达3\" (motor 3).\n\nThe user said \"泵1\" which likely refers to a pump widget, and \"马达3\" likely refers to a motor device or point/tag.\n\nI need to clarify:\n1. What is the widget_id for the pump 1 on the main page?\n2. What is the tag for motor 3?\n\nActually, looking at the bind_point function, it requires:\n- page_id: \"main_page\"\n- widget_id: the ID of the pump widget\n- property: the property to bind (e.g., \"value\", \"status\", \"speed\")\n- tag: the SCADA point tag to bind to\n\nThe user mentioned \"马达3\" which could be a device or a tag. In SCADA context, this could be a tag like \"MOTOR_3\" or \"MOTOR3_STATUS\" etc.\n\nI should ask the user for clarification about:\n1. The exact widget_id for pump 1\n2. The exact tag name for motor 3\n3. What property of the pump should be bound (value, status, speed, etc.)\n\nLet me ask the user for these details."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 30, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 12821, "output_tokens": 657, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 20836.608100002195}, "judge": null}
