alarms 和 manage_points。用户需要为 TI-201 设置 HH alarm（100）和 LL alarm（10），优先级都是 high。点位已经确认存在，类型是 analog。\n\n我需要创建两个报警：一个高高限报警，一个低低限报警。考虑到 TI-201 是模拟量点，我应该使用 create_analog_alarm 动作。我需要为每个报警指定唯一的 ID、tag（TI-201）、high_limit 和 low_limit，以及 priority（high）。\n\n对于 HH 报警，我应该只设置 high_limit 为 100，low_limit 保持 null（或省略）。对于 LL 报警，我应该只设置 low_limit 为 10，high_limit 保持 null。这样两个报警独立工作，分别监控高限和低限。\n\n我可以同时调用两个 manage_alarms，因为它们是独立的。先创建 HH 报警，再创建 LL 报警。我会使用清晰的 ID 命名：alarm_ti201_hh 和 alarm_ti201_ll。\n\n现在调用工具。"}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 2748, "output_tokens": 228, "latency_ms": 7749.065099997097, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我收到错误：low_limit 和 high_limit 参数应该是数字而不是字符串 \"None\"。我需要将它们设置为 null 而不是 \"None\"。JSON Schema 中的 null 应该用 null 值表示，而不是字符串 \"None\"。\n\n让我重新创建这两个报警。对于 HH 报警，high_limit=100，low_limit=null（不设置）。对于 LL 报警，high_limit=null（不设置），low_limit=10。\n\n另外，我需要确保参数类型正确。在 JSON 中，null 应该用 null 值而不是字符串 \"None\"。让我重试。"}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 3050, "output_tokens": 245, "latency_ms": 7762.755600000673, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "参数格式有问题，我需要省略不需要的限值参数而不是传 null。让我重新创建两个报警：", "reasoning": "The error shows that `null` values should not be provided as strings. Let me omit the optional parameters instead of providing null values. The schema shows `high_limit` and `low_limit` have defaults of `null`, so I can just not include them."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 8167, "output_tokens": 481, "latency_ms": 17244.44439999934, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "看起来工具在处理省略参数时有问题。让我尝试显式地为两个限值都提供数值：", "reasoning": "I keep getting schema errors. It seems like the tool is having issues with the parameters. Let me look at the schema more carefully.\n\nThe schema for create_analog_alarm says:\n- high_limit: anyOf: [{type: number}, {type: null}], default: null\n- low_limit: anyOf: [{type: number}, {type: null}], default: null\n\nThe error message says \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" for both low_limit and high_limit.\n\nWait, I think the issue might be that when I omit a parameter, the system is still receiving something it can't parse. Let me try providing explicit number values for both, even if I don't need one of them.\n\nFor HH alarm: high_limit=100, low_limit=0 (or some reasonable value)\nFor LL alarm: high_limit=999 (or some reasonable value), low_limit=10\n\nActually, let me re-read the error more carefully. The error says \"create_analog_alarm.low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - this suggests the parameter is being received as a string somehow.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe I need to explicitly provide both limits as numbers."}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 8767, "output_tokens": 419, "latency_ms": 15306.747099999484, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我换一种方式，提供合理的两个限值作为纯数字：", "reasoning": "I'm getting the same error repeatedly. The error message says \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" for both high_limit and low_limit. This is strange because I'm providing actual numbers.\n\nLet me think about this differently. Maybe the issue is with how the tool is parsing the parameters. The error occurs consistently for the \"opposite\" limit in each call:\n- For HH alarm: error on low_limit (even when I provide -9999)\n- For LL alarm: error on high_limit (even when I provide 9999)\n\nWait, I notice something. The error message always points to the parameter that should be \"null\" or not relevant. Let me try using 0 instead of negative numbers, or maybe try a different approach.\n\nActually, looking at the schema again:\n```\n\"high_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}\n```\n\nThe schema allows null. But when I tried passing null as a string \"None\", it failed. The system seems to have an issue parsing parameters.\n\nLet me try with explicit number values for both limits, using reasonable defaults. For a temperature instrument like TI-201, typical ranges might be -50 to 150 or similar.\n\nLet me try providing both as proper numbers."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 9260, "output_tokens": 158, "latency_ms": 7152.575699998124, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我先只用必填参数试试，看是否能成功创建报警：", "reasoning": "The error keeps happening. Let me try a different approach - maybe the issue is with how the numbers are being passed. Let me try with simpler parameters and see if the basic call works at all.\n\nLooking at the schema more carefully:\n- required: [\"id\", \"tag\", \"action\"]\n- high_limit and low_limit have defaults of null\n\nMaybe I should try with just the required parameters first and see if that works."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 9492, "output_tokens": 247, "latency_ms": 10652.734399998735, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "这看起来是工具后端的一个问题。让我尝试另一种方法，先创建一个基础报警，然后使用 set_threshold 来设置限值：", "reasoning": "This is very strange. Even with just the required parameters, I'm getting a schema error about low_limit. The error says \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" for low_limit.\n\nThis seems like a backend issue with the tool itself. The schema says low_limit has a default of null and is optional, but the backend seems to be trying to parse it as a number.\n\nLet me try one more approach - maybe I need to use integer values instead of decimals, or maybe try a completely different set of parameters. Let me also try the set_threshold action to see if that works differently.\n\nActually, wait - let me try using integer format explicitly for the numbers. Maybe the issue is that the JSON is being parsed in a certain way. Let me try with minimal parameters."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 30, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker