4799998201197, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}, {"turn": 1, "state": "VALIDATE", "visible_tools": [], "visible_count": 0, "selected": "workflow:handlers.validate_project", "action": null, "args": {}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": true, "error_code": "OK", "error_msg": null, "result_data": {"ok": true, "checked_at": "validate_project"}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 0.005000001692678779, "intended_entities": [], "referenced_entities": []}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:d88107776650cb454d9d573d07babb192ac66fb7faa1784b2aff648b26102014", "final_hash": "sha256:d88107776650cb454d9d573d07babb192ac66fb7faa1784b2aff648b26102014", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 1024, "output_tokens": 171, "latency_ms": 9875.256700001046, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "我需要先了解一下现有的点位和脚本情况，确认 PI-201 和 valve1 是否存在，以及它们的数据类型。", "reasoning": "The user wants to create a new global script with an OnEvent trigger. The logic should be: if PI-201 is too high, then set valve1.\n\nBefore creating the script, I need to:\n1. Check what points exist (to verify PI-201 and valve1 exist and understand their types)\n2. Check what scripts already exist (to understand naming conventions)\n\nLet me first query the existing points and scripts to understand the current state."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 7939, "output_tokens": 347, "latency_ms": 12685.1115999998, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "很好！已确认当前项目中存在以下点位：\n- **PI-201**：模拟量 (analog) — 压力指示\n- **valve1**：数字量 (digital) — 阀门控制\n\n目前没有任何脚本。\n\n在创建脚本之前，我需要确认几个细节：\n\n1. **PI-201 的报警阈值是多少？** 即\"过高\"的判断值，比如 `PI-201 > 100`？\n2. **\"置位\" valve1** — 是将 valve1 设为 `true`（打开阀门）还是 `false`（关闭阀门）？通常\"置位\"指设为 `true`，请确认。", "reasoning": "I found:\n- PI-201 is an analog type point (pressure indicator)\n- valve1 is a digital type point (valve control)\n- No existing scripts\n\nNow I need to create an on_event script. The user wants:\n- If PI-201 is too high, then set valve1\n\nI need to ask the user what \"too high\" means - what's the threshold value? Also, I should clarify:\n1. What threshold value for PI-201?\n2. What does \"置位\" mean - set to true (open) or set to false (close)?\n\nActually, let me proceed with reasonable assumptions and ask for clarification. The user said \"过高\" (too high), so I should ask what threshold they want. And \"置位\" in SCADA context typically means setting a digital point to true (1).\n\nLet me ask the user for the threshold value."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 30, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "ScriptConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 8963, "output_tokens": 518, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 22584.81960000063}, "judge": null}
